[h1]Bug Reports[/h1]
Post bugs in this thread only. One bug per reply, so each can be tracked and answered. Questions and suggestions belong in their own threads.

[h2]Before you post[/h2]
[olist]
    [*]Confirm Harmony, ButterLib, UIExtenderEx, and Mod Configuration Menu (MCM) are enabled in the launcher, below them in load order.
    [*]Confirm you are on Bannerlord v1.4.0 through v1.4.8.
    [*]Check whether the bug still happens with every other mod disabled. If it goes away, say which mod brings it back.
    [*]Say which inventory screen it happened in (regular inventory, loot screen, trade, and so on) and which side (left, right, or both).
[/olist]

[h2]Turn on the log[/h2]
Enable "Enable Logging" in the MCM options screen under Inventory Enhancer, then reproduce the bug. The file is at:
[code]Documents\Mount and Blade II Bannerlord\Configs\ModLogs\Inventory Enhancer.log[/code]
Steam comments strip long pastes, so upload the whole file to a paste site or file host and link it rather than pasting only the lines you think matter.

[h2]What to include[/h2]
Copy this template into your reply and fill in every line:
[code]
Mod version:        (the version shown on this Workshop page)
Bannerlord version: (shown in the launcher)
Screen:             (inventory / loot / trade / other)
Sort or filter used: (which category, and which side)
Other mods:         (the full list, or "none")
What I did:
What happened:
What I expected:
Log:                (link to the file, see above)
[/code]

[h2]What happens next[/h2]
Confirmed bugs are fixed in a PATCH update, listed in the Change Notes tab. A reply in this thread will say which version carries the fix. Reports missing the log or the version are answered with a request for them before anything else.

[h2]Not bugs[/h2]
[list]
    [*]An in-game message says a sort or filter failed to apply. This is the mod reporting the failure instead of failing silently; post it here as a bug with the log attached, the message itself is expected behavior, not a separate defect.
    [*]Your sort or filter choices reset when you reopen an inventory. Check "Remember Selections" in MCM; it is off by default.
    [*]The culture filter shows nothing for an item. Items with no culture, or a non-playable one, are expected to match none of the six culture options.
[/list]
